WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.376
[in Russian] "I have made the decision
to carry out

00:00:02.376 --> 00:00:04.459
a special military operation."

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.261
Putin called this a "special military operation".

00:00:13.261 --> 00:00:16.582
But it's clear, this is a full scale invasion.

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:19.321
"There was total panic. Hysteria. Tears.'

00:00:19.321 --> 00:00:22.204
"The flame was higher than the house."

00:00:22.204 --> 00:00:23.514
"We're like, in a cellar."

00:00:23.514 --> 00:00:27.180
"I'm not sure if it's like deep enough to
help us to survive."

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.174
Russian troops and tanks have 
entered Ukraine on all fronts.

00:00:31.174 --> 00:00:35.236
All these cities are under attack, 
including the capital of Kyiv

00:00:35.236 --> 00:00:37.747
which has become Putin’s main target.

00:00:37.747 --> 00:00:41.460
Many are sheltering in basements and 
metro stations across Ukraine.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.370
There have been hundreds of casualties 
and over half a million Ukrainians 

00:00:45.370 --> 00:00:47.902
have been forced to flee their homes.

00:00:47.902 --> 00:00:51.801
This is one of Europe’s largest wars 
since World War II.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:55.782
Since then, Europe’s map has been shaped
by political alliances.

00:00:55.782 --> 00:00:59.794
But now, Putin wants to redraw 
Europe’s map by force.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:16.820
Putin has long claimed Ukraine belongs to
Russia and they are one people.

00:01:17.093 --> 00:01:21.258
"We're not just close neighbors, 
we're one nation."

00:01:21.258 --> 00:01:26.193
But Ukraine is a sovereign nation with its own 
language, culture, and political system.

00:01:26.193 --> 00:01:28.920
And while the two countries 
do have a shared history

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.250
Ukraine has fought hard for its own identity.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.520
Ukraine was part of the Russian Empire in
the 18th and 19th centuries.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:40.478
In 1917, the Russian Revolution 
brought down the empire 

00:01:40.478 --> 00:01:43.382
and the region spiraled into a civil war.

00:01:43.382 --> 00:01:46.045
Ukraine briefly gained independence 
from Russian rule

00:01:46.045 --> 00:01:49.610
but was quickly taken over by the 
newly created Soviet Union

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:52.428
as one of its first republics.

00:01:52.428 --> 00:01:56.176
Over the next decade, the Soviet Union 
brutally expanded its control.

00:01:56.176 --> 00:02:00.803
And by the end of WWII, it forged 
a sphere of influence over here.

00:02:00.803 --> 00:02:03.634
While the west held its influence over here.

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:08.635
Essentially dividing Europe and marking the
beginning of the Cold War.

00:02:08.635 --> 00:02:11.530
The Soviet Union installed communist governments
on their side

00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:13.957
which were easy for them to control.

00:02:13.957 --> 00:02:18.560
But the west developed into democracies 
with capitalist economies.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:23.386
The deep ideological divide fueled distrust
and tensions between the two sides.

00:02:23.386 --> 00:02:27.410
And soon these spheres hardened 
into military alliances.

00:02:28.073 --> 00:02:32.080
In 1949, these countries along, 
with the US and Canada

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:35.490
formed the North Atlantic Treaty Organization,
or NATO

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:38.120
and promised to defend each other from invasion.

00:02:38.614 --> 00:02:43.176
A few years later, these countries joined
the Soviet-led Warsaw Pact alliance.

00:02:43.176 --> 00:02:47.450
And each side built up its military to protect
itself from the other.

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:52.312
Europe remained this way for decades, 
until one side finally collapsed.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:03:02.870
By late 1991, republics like Ukraine began
declaring independence from Soviet domination.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:08.684
The Soviet Union dissolved into 15 independent
countries, including a much weaker Russia.

00:03:08.684 --> 00:03:11.110
And the Soviet sphere of influence disappeared

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:14.540
as many countries overthrew 
their communist governments.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:16.092
Even though the Cold War ended

00:03:16.092 --> 00:03:19.667
the alliance on the other side of Europe 
was still going strong.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:21.971
In fact, it was expanding.

00:03:21.971 --> 00:03:26.757
In 1999, Poland, Hungary, and the Czech Republic
joined NATO.

00:03:26.757 --> 00:03:29.847
In 2004, seven more countries joined.

00:03:29.847 --> 00:03:33.540
That moved NATO into the old Soviet sphere
of influence.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.441
Making NATO's border with Russia
the longest it's ever been.

00:03:37.441 --> 00:03:41.546
Belarus, Ukraine, and Georgia were now the
last post-Soviet countries left 

00:03:41.546 --> 00:03:43.398
between Russia and NATO.

00:03:43.398 --> 00:03:47.599
But Ukraine and Georgia both wanted to join
NATO for a long time.

00:03:47.599 --> 00:03:50.452
And that made them prime targets for Russia.

00:03:51.452 --> 00:03:54.322
Ukraine became a NATO partner in 1994

00:03:54.322 --> 00:03:57.185
which brought them a step closer 
to becoming a member.

00:03:57.799 --> 00:04:00.119
"Ukraine will be in NATO."

00:04:00.119 --> 00:04:03.733
"This is a historic event for our people."

00:04:03.733 --> 00:04:08.486
And in 2013, they were going to sign an association
agreement with the European Union.

00:04:08.486 --> 00:04:10.489
But when it came time to sign the deal

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:13.328
Ukraine’s pro-Russian government refused.

00:04:13.328 --> 00:04:16.793
Instead they chose to strengthen ties 
with Russia.

00:04:16.793 --> 00:04:21.712
After the decision was announced, hundreds
of thousands of protesters took to the streets

00:04:21.712 --> 00:04:23.522
to demand the agreement be signed.

00:04:23.522 --> 00:04:27.480
[chanting] Ukraine is Europe!
Ukraine is Europe!

00:04:30.641 --> 00:04:34.074
After months of peaceful protests, the Ukrainian
president cracked down

00:04:34.074 --> 00:04:36.944
and killed more than 100 people.

00:04:36.944 --> 00:04:42.867
Sparking more protests which eventually drove
the president out of office and the country.

00:04:42.867 --> 00:04:47.208
This meant Putin would lose political influence
over Ukraine.

00:04:47.208 --> 00:04:50.791
So he decided to use force instead.

00:04:50.791 --> 00:04:54.634
First, he invaded and annexed Ukraine’s
Crimean Peninsula.

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:59.074
Then, Russia-backed separatists captured 
the regions of Donetsk and Luhansk

00:04:59.074 --> 00:05:01.714
and declared them independent of Ukraine.

00:05:01.714 --> 00:05:07.271
Since then, Ukraine has been locked in a conflict
with Russia that has killed 14,000 people

00:05:07.271 --> 00:05:10.434
and displaced nearly 2 million people.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:14.134
For nearly eight years, Putin has held on
to these regions

00:05:14.134 --> 00:05:18.494
destabilizing Ukraine, and keeping it from
moving closer to the west.

00:05:18.494 --> 00:05:23.004
But in November 2021, Putin decided 
to go all in.

00:05:23.004 --> 00:05:27.705
Satellite images showed at least 100,000 Russian
troops and military equipment

00:05:27.705 --> 00:05:30.354
piling up along the border of Ukraine.

00:05:30.354 --> 00:05:33.291
Putin repeatedly denied any plans to invade.

00:05:33.291 --> 00:05:37.062
But weeks later, he presented his demands
to the west.

00:05:37.062 --> 00:05:39.806
His main demand was that NATO stop expanding

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:43.644
and move its military borders 
back to where they were in 1997

00:05:43.644 --> 00:05:45.182
away from Russia’s.

00:05:45.182 --> 00:05:47.509
Western leaders rejected his demands.

00:05:47.509 --> 00:05:53.047
Instead, they put forces on standby and reinforced
their military presence in Eastern Europe.

00:05:53.047 --> 00:05:57.238
Back at Ukraine’s border, Russian troops
continued to gather.

00:05:57.238 --> 00:06:03.944
And over here, along its border with Belarus,
Russia began conducting huge military drills.

00:06:03.944 --> 00:06:07.767
On February 21st, the threat of war 
became real.

00:06:07.767 --> 00:06:12.203
"I consider it necessary to take 
a long-overdue decision

00:06:12.203 --> 00:06:15.239
and to immediately recognize the independence

00:06:15.239 --> 00:06:17.774
and sovereignty of the Donesk People's Republic

00:06:17.774 --> 00:06:20.081
and the Lugansk People's Republic."

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.666
His troops immediately crossed the Ukrainian
border into Russian-backed separatist regions

00:06:24.666 --> 00:06:26.887
under the pretense of peacekeeping.

00:06:26.887 --> 00:06:28.971
Ukraine announced a state of emergency

00:06:28.971 --> 00:06:32.571
and President Zelensky made a direct appeal
to the Russian people.

00:06:32.571 --> 00:06:35.588
"A war will take away guarantees from everyone."

00:06:35.588 --> 00:06:40.714
"No one will have security guarantees."

00:06:40.714 --> 00:06:45.574
"Who will suffer the most?
The people."

00:06:45.574 --> 00:06:51.413
"Who doesn't want it the most?
The people."

00:06:51.413 --> 00:06:57.348
"Who can stop it?
The people."

00:06:57.766 --> 00:06:59.905
Hours later on February 24th

00:06:59.905 --> 00:07:05.151
Putin launched a full-scale invasion in Ukraine.

00:07:05.151 --> 00:07:08.047
World leaders have spoken out 
against Russia’s invasion.

00:07:08.047 --> 00:07:13.516
“We condemn this barbaric attack and the
cynical arguments to justify it."

00:07:13.516 --> 00:07:19.749
“This hideous and barbaric venture of Vladimir
Putin must end in failure."

00:07:19.749 --> 00:07:22.458
“Putin chose this war

00:07:22.458 --> 00:07:25.108
and now he and his country will bear the consequences.”

00:07:25.108 --> 00:07:28.195
Anti-war protests have broken out 
around the world.

00:07:28.195 --> 00:07:31.562
Including in Russia, despite the risk of arrest.

00:07:31.562 --> 00:07:33.698
Neighboring nations have opened their borders

00:07:33.698 --> 00:07:36.868
as hundreds of thousands of Ukrainians 
attempt to flee.

00:07:36.868 --> 00:07:40.432
NATO’s response force has been activated
for the first time in history.

00:07:40.432 --> 00:07:43.992
And the US has sent additional troops 
to eastern Europe.

00:07:43.992 --> 00:07:47.935
But in many ways, the world is treading carefully.

00:07:47.935 --> 00:07:51.796
Putin controls the world’s largest arsenal
of nuclear weapons

00:07:51.796 --> 00:07:54.624
and has already threatened anyone 
who might interfere.

00:07:54.624 --> 00:07:57.562
"Whoever tries to stop us

00:07:57.562 --> 00:08:00.848
should know that Russia's response 
will be immediate."

00:08:00.848 --> 00:08:03.731
"And will lead to such consequences

00:08:03.731 --> 00:08:08.451
that you have never faced in your history."

00:08:08.451 --> 00:08:12.622
So countries around the world are imposing
some of the harshest economic sanctions 

00:08:12.622 --> 00:08:14.186
to slow Putin down.

00:08:14.186 --> 00:08:18.148
And sending tons of military aid 
to support Ukraine.

00:08:18.148 --> 00:08:23.606
For now, Russian forces keep pushing deeper,
but Ukraine is fighting back.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.495
"We are all here protecting 
our independence, our country."

00:08:26.495 --> 00:08:29.071
"And we are going to continue to do so."

